  {
    "url": "https://stripe.com/en-mt/resources/more/mandatory-electronic-invoicing-spain",
    "title": "Mandatory electronic invoicing in Spain | Stripe",
    "snippet": "Nov 4, 2025         The Create and Grow Law imposes the most stringent legal requirements for electronic invoicing in Spain, although other laws complement the regulatory framework. The following are some of the most important obligations: Reporting on invoice status Both parties need to report on the status of their invoices: issued, received, paid or overdue. To illustrate, when paying suppliers, you must explicitly state that you have paid the invoices. Providing free copies The person or company getting an e-invoice needs to be able to request a copy at no additional cost.   Summarize",
    "published": null
  },
  {
    "url": "https://www.ey.com/en_gl/technical/tax-alerts/spanish-government-approves-royal-decree-implementing-mandatory-b2b-electronic-invoicing",
    "title": "Spain approves mandatory B2B e-invoicing decree | EY - Global",
    "snippet": "On 24 March 2026, the Spanish Council of Ministers approved the Royal Decree implementing the mandatory business-to-business (B2B) electronic invoicing system in Law 18/2022 (the Create and Grow Law), which completes the regulatory framework required to implement the new system. The Royal Decree establishes the legal and operational framework for electronic invoicing between businesses and ...   Summarize",
    "published": null
  },
  {
    "url": "https://kpmg.com/us/en/taxnewsflash/news/2026/03/spain-e-invoicing-mandate-b2b.html",
    "title": "Spain: Council of Ministers approves e-invoicing mandate for B2B ...",
    "snippet": "Mar 1, 2026         The B2B e-invoicing mandate is designed to address this challenge by providing full traceability of the invoicing cycle. By electronically recording when each invoice is issued, accepted, and paid, companies will have greater control over their cash flows, and the tax authority will be able to monitor compliance with payment deadlines.   Summarize",
    "published": null
  },
  {
    "url": "https://www.heropay.eu/en/blog/electronic-invoicing-spain/",
    "title": "Electronic invoicing in Spain: everything you need to know about...",
    "snippet": "Apr 15, 2026         Legal requirements for electronic invoicing in Spain.Electronic invoicing for foreign companies in Spain. Non-resident companies should check whether they are affected by Spain's e-invoicing obligation. Regulations distinguish between companies with a permanent establishment in Spain and those operating internationally with no local presence.   Summarize",
    "published": null
  },
  {
    "url": "https://getrenn.com/blog/mandatory-electronic-invoice",
    "title": "Mandatory Electronic Invoice Spain: Dates, Formats & Compliance",
    "snippet": "B2B e-invoicing becomes mandatory once the Ministerial Order is published. Covers deadlines by company size, UBL and Facturae formats, Verifactu overlap, and the compliance checklist.   Summarize",
    "published": null
  },
  {
    "url": "https://informatecdigital.com/en/Mandatory-electronic-invoicing-regulations--deadlines-and-how-to-prepare/",
    "title": "Mandatory electronic invoicing: deadlines, law and requirements",
    "snippet": "With the Create and Grow Law, e-invoicing is extended to all business-to-business (B2B) transactions. It is expected that, once the 1 or 2-year periods following the Ministerial Order have elapsed, all private Spanish businesses are required to use electronic invoicing when the recipient is a businessperson or professional established in Spain.   Summarize",
    "published": null
  },
  {
    "url": "https://www.banqup.com/resources/blog/10-essential-facts-on-spain-s-broad-invoicing-mandates",
    "title": "Spain's B2B E-invoicing Law Facts | Blog - Banqup",
    "snippet": "Mar 23, 2026         Spain has approved the Royal Degree under the Crea y Crece law, making B2B electronic invoicing mandatory for companies and professionals. Discover more.   Summarize",
    "published": null
  },
  {
    "url": "https://edicomgroup.com/blog/electronic-invoicing-will-be-mandatory-for-spanish-companies",
    "title": "Mandatory Electronic Invoicing B2B in Spain | EDICOM",
    "snippet": "The initiative to implement electronic invoicing between businesses in Spain is described within the \"Crea y Crece\" Law, which was created in September 2022. This law designates electronic invoicing as the exclusive method for conducting commercial transactions between companies and self-employed individuals in Spain.   Summarize",
    "published": null
  },
  {
    "url": "https://blogs.opentext.com/e-invoicing-mandates-and-updates-spain/",
    "title": "e-Invoicing mandates and updates: Spain - OpenText Blogs",
    "snippet": "Apr 15, 2026         Scope of the Spanish B2B E-Invoicing Mandate: All companies and professionals required to issue invoices under Spanish law will be obliged to do so electronically. Some excluded transactions include simplified invoices and cases where there is no legal obligation to issue an invoice under Spanish rules. The mandate is for domestic e-Invoices only and does not apply if one of the parties is not established within Spanish territory.   Summarize",
    "published": null
  }
]
